{"seq":12,"trial_id":"v03-installer-dev-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T15:24:42.185Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0446febfde6286e8237c280950b8696074cbb4e98f204984f5e0951680950cdc","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**: from `dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday` (\"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\", 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct about gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments at the Eau Claire yard. The note says support patched it and the 04:00 shift cleared on 5 Oct.\n2. **#4419**: from `dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet` (\"Moss: North cheat sheet\", undated). Thea logged it about gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nI also saw #4419 in a 14 Jul 2025 note, `dev/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap`, which Marcus Lindqvist wrote rather than Moss. It describes a Gate 3 printer lag fix under that number, so the number may be reused or the note may be mislabelled. Check it before you put both in the weekly notes.\n\nSome caveats:\n- The brain search is keyword-only, because semantic search isn't enabled here. A ticket phrased differently could still be missing, so this list may not be complete.\n- I didn't count the Quarendon Freightways references in the cheat sheet. The note says that company isn't a Pemberline customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
